WEBVTT

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:19.200
<i>C'mon, morning's here--time to be on our way</i>

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:24.700
<i>Smiling faces, courage,</i>
<i>we're bustin' out: glory days!</i>

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:29.830
<i>You ready or not? Ready or not, go!</i>
<i>No turning back: this trip is nonfiction</i>

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:35.080
<i>You ready or not? Ready or not, go!</i>
<i>It's now or never, the real deal: Ready, and... action!</i>

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:40.540
<i>Harsh winds that make us hesitate,</i>
<i>nights spent crying our eyes out</i>

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:45.790
<i>They're not necessarily bad things (not bad)</i>

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:51.500
<i>Just like the power in a spring:</i>
<i>the harder we're pushed</i>

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:55.040
<i>The higher we can fly</i>

00:00:55.040 --> 00:01:05.580
<i>Face the far-off distance</i>
<i>and aim for the horizon: rising sun</i>

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:10.870
<i>Holding our hands up to that morning sun</i>

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:21.250
<i>Our shared feelings brought us together--</i>
<i>we're not alone anymore</i>

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:27.450
<i>And so we're on this brilliant voyage</i>

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:34.250
<i>Smiling faces, courage,</i>
<i>we're bustin' out: glory days!</i>

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:41.370
Under the rule of Ei Sei,
the King who worked toward unification,

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:45.370
the Kingdom of Chin launched an invasion
of the neighboring land of Gi.

00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:48.660
Ou Hon, Mou Ten, and Shin:

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:52.370
these bold soldiers and aspiring
great generals were together here now,

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:55.790
ready to usher in a brand-new age!

00:01:55.790 --> 00:01:57.160
So you're Shin...

00:01:58.870 --> 00:02:01.580
You look just as I'd imagined.

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:03.450
You were once a servant, yes?

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:08.450
I, Kaku Bi, was once a servant, too.

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:13.750
I thought I'd step in to offer my help, but...

00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:16.700
...I see I should just mind my own business.

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:21.910
This unit is on the right track.
Just keep going.

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:27.370
Don't let those nobles beat you, Shin!

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:35.200
Commander Kaku Bi, a moment?

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:50.500
Kaku Bi, sir!

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:52.120
Commander!

00:02:57.080 --> 00:02:59.370
Commander Kaku Bi!

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:01.750
Commander...

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:12.580
How... how could this happen?

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:18.120
He was only just talkin' to us...

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:22.040
Commander Kaku Bi...

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:27.250
You watch... I'm gonna avenge you--
you can count on it!

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:34.950
There must be Gi assassins hiding somewhere!

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:40.040
They might still be nearby!
We should look, too, Shin!

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:41.450
Damn right we should!

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:46.330
Spread out in teams of five!
Leave no stone unturned--

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:49.500
we're gonna find the bastard
who killed Commander Kaku Bi!

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:56.410
Terrible news!

00:03:57.700 --> 00:04:00.000
What? They find 'em already?

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:03.910
It's not just Kaku Bi!

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:05.580
Commander Hi Shi--

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:07.830
and Commander Bako Ku have been slain, too!

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:10.330
What?!

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:11.830
Thousand-man commanders...

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:13.200
...all three of them!

00:04:16.830 --> 00:04:18.290
What the hell...

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:20.950
What's goin' on?

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:52.370
Let's see... huh?

00:04:52.370 --> 00:04:54.450
That was Bako Ku I killed earlier?

00:04:56.120 --> 00:04:58.750
So who's this, then?

00:04:58.750 --> 00:04:59.910
Rin Ko, sir?

00:04:59.910 --> 00:05:05.540
It's about time to move out.
The Chin are growing restless.

00:05:05.540 --> 00:05:08.910
Fine, fine... I think I'll go with <i>him</i> next.

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:13.660
All right--

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:19.660
I'll take down one or two more,
then we can call it a night.

00:05:20.410 --> 00:05:25.410
"The Air of a General"

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:32.080
Now Commander Riku's been slain!

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:36.000
We can't dismiss this as the work
of a mere enemy remnant!

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:38.620
There is a skilled assassin among us--
make no mistake.

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:43.370
We're in an unfamiliar place...
and with night falling,

00:05:43.370 --> 00:05:45.620
we're in real danger!

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:46.830
Remain calm!

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:50.660
Triple the size of the security patrol!

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:52.120
Sir!

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:53.870
Close the gates up tight--

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:55.330
let no one through!

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:56.410
Yes, sir!

00:05:58.330 --> 00:05:59.580
General Ra Gen!

00:06:03.330 --> 00:06:05.080
Ah, young sir!

00:06:07.410 --> 00:06:09.580
We have a rat among us, I see.

00:06:09.580 --> 00:06:14.080
Yes, and one with particularly nasty fangs.

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:17.120
We've already lost six
thousand-man commanders.

00:06:18.200 --> 00:06:19.330
Six?!

00:06:20.250 --> 00:06:22.160
The commanding general is safe?

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:25.870
He is. Haku Rou is naturally cautious,

00:06:25.870 --> 00:06:29.080
and we've increased his guards as well.

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:32.500
You ought to be careful yourself, young sir.

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:34.500
The Gaku Ka Force may have but 300 members,

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:37.200
but you are ranked high enough
to command a thousand.

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:39.750
The assassin could well come after you.

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:42.790
Yes, about that...

00:06:42.790 --> 00:06:45.120
Doesn't it make you feel uneasy?

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:51.540
From what I hear, the slain
commanders were all powerhouses

00:06:51.540 --> 00:06:53.580
in the main unit.

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:56.790
They're obviously going after the big guns.

00:06:57.950 --> 00:07:01.330
It's almost as though a certain Gi general

00:07:01.330 --> 00:07:04.830
is laying the groundwork
for a huge war down the road.

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:23.450
The Mou clan has grown more secure
in your generation, young sir.

00:07:23.450 --> 00:07:27.410
But you are overthinking this.

00:07:27.410 --> 00:07:32.410
There are no generals in Gi
skilled enough for such plotting,

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:34.290
not since Go Kei died.

00:07:34.290 --> 00:07:38.910
This business is simply
a rogue Gi soldier turned assassin

00:07:38.910 --> 00:07:43.950
here in Kin Rikan,
striking back the best he can.

00:07:43.950 --> 00:07:48.000
He targets thousand-man commanders
because the higher ranks

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:49.410
are better protected.

00:07:51.540 --> 00:07:55.790
Security is light for thousand-man
commanders--that much is true...

00:07:55.790 --> 00:07:58.950
But please be cautious, General Ra Gen.

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:03.870
As hard as it is to lose
these skilled commanders,

00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:07.540
there is no substitute for you.

00:08:07.540 --> 00:08:12.870
If you were slain, General Mou Gou's army

00:08:12.870 --> 00:08:14.620
would be greatly diminished.

00:08:16.290 --> 00:08:17.750
Understood.

00:08:17.750 --> 00:08:20.660
But never fear: The assassin
will be caught and beheaded

00:08:20.660 --> 00:08:22.000
this very night!

00:08:31.830 --> 00:08:36.700
But in the end, the Chin army
was unable to apprehend the culprit.

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:45.040
Mou Gou's army lost eight thousand-men
commanders in that single night.

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:52.950
Three days later,

00:08:55.080 --> 00:08:58.910
Mou Gou's army was preparing
to take their next castle

00:08:58.910 --> 00:09:00.950
under the strictest of conditions.

00:09:13.250 --> 00:09:15.000
Look, sir!

00:09:15.830 --> 00:09:18.750
All those heavy infantry
surrounding the main camp,

00:09:18.750 --> 00:09:22.660
where General Mou Gou is!

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:25.910
Perhaps your advice worked <i>too</i> well, young sir.

00:09:25.910 --> 00:09:30.450
Now no one can approach Haku Rou,
be they assassin or assistant!

00:09:32.290 --> 00:09:36.750
This is the same tightened security
we'd have during a pitched battle.

00:09:37.540 --> 00:09:40.450
Has Grandfather picked up on something, too?

00:09:40.450 --> 00:09:43.000
Even that wall around
Ra Gen is impenetrable...

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:46.950
No way will an assassin
come after them like this.

00:09:46.950 --> 00:09:49.580
It's far too impractical.

00:10:05.950 --> 00:10:06.950
Huh?

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:11.910
For a second there, I...

00:10:13.370 --> 00:10:14.580
What's up, Shin?

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:19.450
It's like I felt a chill...

00:10:21.830 --> 00:10:23.040
Hey, Shin!

00:10:24.830 --> 00:10:26.080
What's wrong?

00:10:28.540 --> 00:10:32.330
It's nothin'. C'mon.

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:04.620
What's the meaning of this, Ren Pa?

00:11:04.620 --> 00:11:09.330
I hear one of your associates
has gone off to slay Chin commanders

00:11:09.330 --> 00:11:11.290
with only 300 men.

00:11:11.290 --> 00:11:14.370
I could have given him
thousands of troops if you'd just asked.

00:11:14.370 --> 00:11:19.580
Rin Ko would never misjudge his own ability.

00:11:19.580 --> 00:11:24.330
If he says 300, then 300 it is.

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:29.660
B-But it would take 300 troops
all they had to chip away at one camp!

00:11:29.660 --> 00:11:33.950
Killing commanders of an army
more than ten thousand strong? Never!

00:11:33.950 --> 00:11:37.830
And Rin Ko--he's that young man
with the feminine appearance, no?

00:11:39.370 --> 00:11:40.370
Ah...

00:11:42.080 --> 00:11:45.870
Do you mean to say the spear
I have thrown is a light one?

00:11:45.870 --> 00:11:48.790
N-Not at all.

00:11:48.790 --> 00:11:53.540
Excellent. Since you judge only by appearances,

00:11:53.540 --> 00:11:55.870
allow me to explain so you will understand.

00:11:56.830 --> 00:11:59.910
Are you familiar with Chin's six great generals?

00:12:01.830 --> 00:12:02.870
Yes, of course I--

00:12:02.870 --> 00:12:04.160
No,

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:05.830
you are <i>not</i> !

00:12:05.830 --> 00:12:06.830
What?!

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:10.700
Wh-What do you mean, Ren Pa?

00:12:11.660 --> 00:12:13.080
Ren Pa?

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:15.040
Indeed...

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:20.200
...it felt as though burning lead
was being driven into my belly

00:12:21.910 --> 00:12:26.790
whenever I faced off against
troops led by those six great generals.

00:12:31.200 --> 00:12:35.620
No matter how many times we fought,
each time brought pressure so great

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:39.500
as to crush my insides into paste...

00:12:40.580 --> 00:12:47.000
Especially Ou Ki's army.
His multilayered defensive formation

00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:49.290
was a veritable iron wall!

00:12:50.790 --> 00:12:54.700
Attempting to take his head
would be like stripping naked

00:12:54.700 --> 00:12:57.790
and bashing yourself against that barrier.

00:12:58.830 --> 00:13:00.000
And yet,

00:13:01.540 --> 00:13:03.750
Rin Ko did it!

00:13:07.790 --> 00:13:12.290
What's more, having put
a chink in that metal wall,

00:13:12.290 --> 00:13:14.370
he then crossed blades...

00:13:19.750 --> 00:13:22.540
...with Ou Ki beyond it!

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:31.950
So you understand.

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:37.000
If Rin Ko says 300, 300 is enough.

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:43.500
Once he has been loosed from my grasp,
no one can stop him!

00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:05.030
"Shin"

00:14:08.290 --> 00:14:11.120
No! General, sir!

00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:12.370
It's the general!

00:14:12.370 --> 00:14:13.750
General Ra Gen!

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:17.700
Not General Ra Gen!

00:14:17.700 --> 00:14:21.160
General Ra Gen is slain!

00:14:21.160 --> 00:14:22.790
What?!

00:14:22.790 --> 00:14:26.250
Impossible! How on earth--

00:14:26.250 --> 00:14:29.040
The assassin has troops laying in ambush!

00:14:29.040 --> 00:14:31.160
Some 300 of them!

00:14:31.160 --> 00:14:32.410
Here they come!

00:14:32.410 --> 00:14:35.290
We're up against a 300-man unit!

00:14:35.290 --> 00:14:36.870
Over there!

00:14:35.290 --> 00:14:38.120
A 300-man unit?

00:14:36.870 --> 00:14:38.120
They went that way!

00:14:39.750 --> 00:14:41.660
They went down the slope!

00:14:41.660 --> 00:14:44.540
You down there--surround them!

00:14:44.540 --> 00:14:47.790
Don't let them get away!

00:14:47.790 --> 00:14:49.370
It's them!

00:14:49.370 --> 00:14:52.660
The 300-man unit that killed General Ra Gen!

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:55.450
They must be who killed General Kaku Bi, then!

00:15:02.160 --> 00:15:04.580
Time for us to get revenge

00:15:05.910 --> 00:15:07.660
for General Kaku Bi!

00:15:11.000 --> 00:15:13.410
What shall I do, Rin Ko, sir?

00:15:13.410 --> 00:15:17.450
Forget about the small fry.
Drive them out in front and keep going.

00:15:41.620 --> 00:15:42.620
He stopped it?!

00:15:51.370 --> 00:15:52.540
Sir!

00:15:52.540 --> 00:15:53.540
Commander!

00:15:57.200 --> 00:15:59.330
L-Let go, you--

00:15:59.330 --> 00:16:01.580
Ow! Let go, dammit!

00:16:10.370 --> 00:16:12.660
This guy's grip is insane!

00:16:13.790 --> 00:16:14.700
You bastard!

00:16:14.700 --> 00:16:15.790
Let me--

00:16:23.160 --> 00:16:24.330
Son of a bitch!

00:16:26.080 --> 00:16:28.000
Quit screwin' around!

00:16:28.700 --> 00:16:29.700
Huh?

00:16:40.950 --> 00:16:42.040
Rin Ko, sir?

00:16:42.040 --> 00:16:45.200
Go on ahead. I'll be along shortly.

00:16:46.200 --> 00:16:47.250
Rin Ko...?

00:16:49.120 --> 00:16:51.120
Now that's strange...

00:16:51.120 --> 00:16:54.160
You're not at all afraid of my bloodlust.

00:16:54.160 --> 00:16:56.500
You even dodged my sword!

00:16:56.500 --> 00:16:58.370
Am I getting rusty?

00:16:59.620 --> 00:17:02.660
Or are you just that strong?

00:17:03.830 --> 00:17:04.830
Which is it?

00:17:07.700 --> 00:17:09.750
I'm just that strong, obviously!

00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:11.370
Right?

00:17:11.370 --> 00:17:12.950
And your name?

00:17:12.950 --> 00:17:14.660
Shin of the Hi Shin Unit!

00:17:16.910 --> 00:17:18.120
How very straightforward!

00:17:24.290 --> 00:17:26.580
Hmm? You're not in here.

00:17:26.580 --> 00:17:29.450
Shin of the Hi Shin Unit, was it?

00:17:29.450 --> 00:17:31.870
Then I guess I don't need to be killing you.

00:17:34.750 --> 00:17:37.040
It's your lucky day!

00:17:37.040 --> 00:17:38.580
Bye now.

00:17:39.910 --> 00:17:43.950
Wait just a damn minute!
Are you the one who killed Kaku Bi?

00:17:49.410 --> 00:17:53.200
Well, what do you know? I sure did!

00:17:53.200 --> 00:17:58.040
Oh, right! The turn-and-slash job!

00:17:58.040 --> 00:17:59.910
Why, you--

00:18:10.620 --> 00:18:12.200
He did it again!

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:15.870
It's been a while
since I've sparred so seriously.

00:18:19.540 --> 00:18:21.200
Seems like despite his age,

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:23.700
this kid has quite a few battles under his belt.

00:18:25.660 --> 00:18:28.330
A shallow one. So he dodged that, too.

00:18:38.910 --> 00:18:42.370
Dear me! Isn't <i>this</i> a surprise!

00:18:43.580 --> 00:18:45.200
It's ever so faint,

00:18:45.200 --> 00:18:48.660
but this boy already has
the air of a general about him--

00:18:49.790 --> 00:18:55.870
more so than the thousand-man
commanders I've been killing.

00:18:55.870 --> 00:18:59.410
So even Chin has its promising young buds...

00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:04.750
My lord would be eager
to see how he turns out,

00:19:04.750 --> 00:19:07.160
but I'm afraid I don't much care about that.

00:19:20.450 --> 00:19:24.040
So sorry--any enemy I see
must be pulled up by the roots.

00:19:40.290 --> 00:19:42.910
Commanderrr!

00:19:42.910 --> 00:19:44.540
Rescue Commander Shin!

00:19:44.540 --> 00:19:45.870
We're coming!

00:19:45.870 --> 00:19:47.290
Shiiin!

00:19:47.290 --> 00:19:48.330
It's them!

00:19:54.290 --> 00:19:56.700
Wait! Who the hell <i>are</i> you?!

00:19:56.700 --> 00:20:00.160
You act like an assassin...
but you're a 300-man commander?

00:20:03.290 --> 00:20:09.450
I do have 300 men at the moment,
but I'm no 300-man commander.

00:20:09.450 --> 00:20:12.040
There've been times I've led a thousand,

00:20:12.040 --> 00:20:13.330
even ten thousand.

00:20:15.950 --> 00:20:18.750
I'm a full-fledged general.

00:20:18.750 --> 00:20:21.790
What? A general?!

00:20:21.790 --> 00:20:23.200
Bullshit!

00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:26.950
A twisted kid like you could never be a general!

00:20:26.950 --> 00:20:28.950
A twisted kid? You wound me!

00:20:29.950 --> 00:20:32.660
Despite all appearances, I'm in my thirties.

00:20:32.660 --> 00:20:34.790
Th-Thirties?!

00:20:36.450 --> 00:20:38.870
I think that's enough for today.

00:20:40.200 --> 00:20:44.410
Your comrades seem
to idolize you. Good for you.

00:20:45.200 --> 00:20:49.250
People like that tend to be
beloved by the heavens, too.

00:20:49.250 --> 00:20:50.250
The heavens?

00:20:51.540 --> 00:20:53.910
No matter how talented or powerful you may be,

00:20:53.910 --> 00:20:56.410
without a touch of luck from above,

00:20:56.410 --> 00:20:59.080
you'll only meet an early end along your path.

00:21:02.330 --> 00:21:04.540
I've seen it happen to plenty of military men.

00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:09.870
Like, oh, I don't know...
those slain thousand-man commanders?

00:21:09.870 --> 00:21:11.500
<i>You</i> did that!

00:21:14.540 --> 00:21:16.830
There are so few...

00:21:16.830 --> 00:21:20.500
Only a handful of generals
are adored by the heavens.

00:21:45.580 --> 00:21:50.700
Hang on--why am I telling <i>you</i> this?

00:21:51.830 --> 00:21:53.700
Ooh, right:

00:21:58.370 --> 00:22:00.910
Because I thought the way he shone

00:22:00.910 --> 00:22:02.700
somehow

00:22:02.700 --> 00:22:05.540
reminded me of them.

00:22:16.250 --> 00:22:17.790
Shin of the Hi Shin Unit...

00:22:19.290 --> 00:22:22.540
I'll be adding you to my list.

00:22:26.870 --> 00:22:27.870
Wait!

00:22:38.000 --> 00:22:40.660
I'll let you go just this once.

00:22:40.660 --> 00:22:43.580
If we should meet again...

00:22:43.580 --> 00:22:46.410
...I <i>will</i> take your life.

00:22:48.790 --> 00:22:49.700
--Commander!
--Shin!

00:22:49.700 --> 00:22:53.620
--Sir!
--Shin! Are you okay? Shin!

00:22:54.580 --> 00:22:56.750
So the bastard got away...

00:22:56.750 --> 00:22:59.580
What should we do, Shin--go after him?

00:23:02.830 --> 00:23:05.410
A general adored by the heavens...

00:23:07.870 --> 00:23:08.870
Shin?

00:23:18.040 --> 00:23:19.450
The hell's <i>that</i> ?

00:23:22.830 --> 00:23:31.370
<i>I'm dreaming of you, just like back then</i>

00:23:31.370 --> 00:23:39.830
<i>Trusting, unafraid of anything</i>

00:23:39.830 --> 00:23:48.080
<i>Your words that I always remember</i>

00:23:48.080 --> 00:23:56.540
<i>Are getting fainter,</i>
<i>mixed up, about to disappear</i>

00:23:56.540 --> 00:24:01.500
<i>I go crazy trying to make them out</i>

00:24:01.500 --> 00:24:05.830
<i>Barefoot still, I'd lost my way</i>

00:24:05.830 --> 00:24:10.080
<i>It's okay to stop</i>

00:24:10.080 --> 00:24:14.250
<i>But even if I go after you,</i>
<i>if I hold out my hand</i>

00:24:14.250 --> 00:24:17.500
<i>Don't respond just yet</i>

00:24:17.500 --> 00:24:22.700
<i>But until I forget, don't change</i>

00:24:22.700 --> 00:24:26.870
<i>I ask this of you, and yet</i>

00:24:26.870 --> 00:24:34.200
<i>Like a long-awaited morning, it's starting again</i>

00:24:34.200 --> 00:24:37.700
<i>And I still remember</i>

00:24:52.000 --> 00:24:58.010
"Next Episode Preview"

00:25:02.000 --> 00:25:07.020
"The Great General at Midnight"
